{"kind":"report","text":"Design complete for both recurring write-boundary failures. No implementation was made.\n\nHEAD NEWS. Use the review request, not the review promise, as the exclusive lower bound. The reproduced 0608526d blocker 3a040814 was sequenced after its review request but before the review promise; a promise-only window would repeat that failure. A promise counts as seeing earlier news only when it directly cites that exact event.\n\nAt each guarded snapshot, internal/reviewguard scans state statements sequenced after the review request. A statement is head-news only when a structured body.head or body.commit exactly equals the full reviewed Git object ID, or when its direct rests_on names the review request, review promise, a supplied artifact, or an effective artifact whose structured commit equals the reviewed head. Full sha1 and sha256 object IDs are valid. Do not parse abbreviated hashes, prose, or path@commit strings; structured artifact path and commit plus its canonical event ID are the path@commit case. Include matched ineffective, retired, and undefined-kind records and show their decision, because this is an attention guard rather than an authority judgment. Existing standing and staleness checks continue to judge semantic force.\n\nMissing news does not create an absolute veto: it refuses until the reviewer explicitly acknowledges every matched event. Add repeatable CLI --ack-head-news EVENT and MCP ack_head_news. Reject missing, duplicate, and extraneous acknowledgments. Artifact citations already in the verdict count once. Append unique acknowledgments to verdict rests_on, record body.head_news_acknowledged as a canonical sequence-ordered JSON array, and record body.review_frontier as the exact workroom frontier event observed, including when the news set is empty. Acknowledgment means seen, not resolved; the review text records the judgment. Promise + request + artifacts + acknowledgments must remain within intent.MaxCausalReferences and overflow refuses without truncation.\n\nDiscovery, exact-set validation, canonical encoding, and act construction live once in internal/reviewguard; gs review and the MCP review tool only parse arguments. Every repeated basis read includes the news set/digest. The final write is bound to the exact observed frontier; movement reruns preflight and exposes newly arrived news. Exact idempotent replay is recognized before new admission checks, while the same key with changed acknowledgments remains a conflict.\n\nWRITE ADMISSION. Undefined state kinds refuse before signing with no override. A command-shaped mistake points to its dedicated route: ratify, supersede, and review use gs or MCP commands/tools; another absent kind lists the active vocabulary and says a ratified kind-def must establish it. Current custom kinds remain valid.\n\nGeneric state refuses, with no override, only when kind=report and body.verdict or body.status is approved or changes-requested. It points to gs review or MCP review. Canonical review paths carry a process-local GuardedReview marker; the shared builder writes reserved body.review_path=reviewguard@1. Generic state cannot supply reserved admission fields.\n\nA state resting on a basis already retired or stale refuses by default. Effective supersession acts remain advisory because citing the retirement itself can be intentional. The explicit rare-case escape is CLI --allow-dead-basis / MCP allow_dead_basis; it signs body.dead_basis_override=true. Reject direct attempts to spoof the reserved field. The override neither removes staleness nor grants authority; rests_on already names the exact overridden events.\n\nOne Workroom admission function in internal/app serves CLI state/batch, MCP state, and canonical review paths. Authoritative evaluation occurs for a genuinely new submission after idempotency replay detection and against the exact pre-sequence frontier. Add a generic post-dedup application callback to the kernel sequencing path; the kernel schedules it but learns no Workroom semantics. On CAS movement the application guard reevaluates. Batch preflights every act before its first append.\n\nCOMPATIBILITY. Do not change historical fold decisions or replay: old undefined kinds, hand-filed verdicts, and dead-basis filings remain visible exactly as recorded. Exact retries still replay after the world moves. The open string body already carries the reserved fields, so this design needs no schema or fold-profile bump. Architecture documentation must record the generic layer-2 admission callback and layer-5 Workroom policy.\n\nTESTS. Cover structured full-hash and direct-basis news matching for sha1/sha256; ignore prose, short hashes, and raw path@commit; reproduce both historical windows; all acknowledgment set errors, overlap deduplication, canonical order, capacity, and mutations at every read and after confirmation; CLI/MCP body parity and MCP schema; idempotent replay versus changed-intent conflict. Cover undefined/custom kinds, both verdict-shaped fields, guarded review, reserved-field spoofing, retired/stale/live/unknown/supersession bases, override recording, zero-depth refusals, batch atomicity, resident and degraded paths, post-dedup callback ordering, CAS reevaluation, and legacy refold goldens.\n\nARCHITECTURE: layers 2, 5, and 7; the kernel remains semantic-free. SECURITY: any roster actor can create head-news, so explicit acknowledgment preserves progress while preventing unread correction; errors are bounded and never echo arbitrary body text; the signed dead-basis override is visible but confers no authority. SIMPLIFICATION: one reviewguard, one admission function, one existing dead-basis classifier, no prose parser, and no second fold rule."}